{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (multimodal, pca_n2000, multiprofile, avgpool, concat) achieves 0.629 acc, while config_009 (image_only, multiprofile, ViT-L, avgpool) achieves only 0.332 acc. This large gap suggests RNA is the dominant signal, but we cannot yet quantify how much the image modality actually contributes to the multimodal model. Question: config_018 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) is the cleanest single-variable ablation of config_001—it removes only the image modality while keeping the same RNA encoder, profile setting, and aggregation. This directly isolates the image contribution. Why best: With only two experiments done, the highest-uncertainty design question is whether the image modality adds meaningful value or is largely redundant. The answer determines whether future budget should be spent optimizing image encoders/fusion or RNA encoders/aggregation. Combined with the existing image_only baseline (config_009), this gives both unimodal baselines needed to interpret all future multimodal results. No other single experiment reduces this fundamental uncertainty as efficiently."
}

